{
 "name": "m21mix_v3",
 "description": "m21mix_v2 plus the list sets (2026-11-23): questions whose answer needs several far values \u2014 all the values of one thing, and several facts asked for in one question (scripts/build_reasoning_rows.py --only list_16k,list_64k). They take 3 % of the 16k stage and 5 % of the 64k stage, from the `pdfs` share; every other source, weight, row length, token budget and every evaluation set is v2's, copied shard for shard. Why: every planted-fact question of v2 has one value for an answer, and the 150M models trained on it write one far value and stop or repeat it (root-cause probe scripts/concept_use_probe.py, 2026-11-23). E38 mix, version 2 (2026-11-14): m21mix_v1 with the stage-1 web half from NVIDIA's curated Nemotron-CC (High-Quality pages and their Diverse-QA rewrites, the 'high-quality subset' of arXiv 2412.02595) and Nemotron-CC-Math 4plus in place of FineWeb-Edu and FineMath; the web replay of the long stages from Nemotron-CC High-Quality. Every other source is v1's, copied shard for shard. The three Nemotron-CC sources are gated: the build reads HF_TOKEN from AWS Secrets Manager (mrcogito/hf-token). E38 pretraining mix, SmolLM2 tokenizer. Built by scripts/build_m21_mix.py (on a node: infra/aws/jobs/m21_data_build.sh). target_tokens = TRAIN tokens to build per source; a phase's weights are shares of that phase's tokens. fineweb_edu and dclm_edu serve the trunk and the later phases: their targets cover the sum, and the manifest writer gives later phases the last shards (shard token counts are in each done.json). Every Hub source was checked public and ungated without a token on 2026-11-14.",
